# modules/sast/rules/injection.rules - docs/DESIGN.md §6.3 "injection.rules
# (language-agnostic sinks)" seed catalog: OS-command concatenation, SQL
# string concatenation, CRLF/header injection, host-header trust, template
# injection sinks, unsafe redirect, mass-assignment, XXE.

id: SAST-INJ-OS_COMMAND-01
title: OS command built from a shell that trusts its own arguments
severity: critical
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-78
owasp: A03:2021
pattern: (os\.system\(|subprocess\.(call|run|Popen)\([^)]*shell[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*True|child_process\.exec\(|Runtime\.getRuntime\(\)\.exec\()
dialect: ere
tags: static
tags: quick
remediation: Pass arguments as a list/array to a non-shell exec call instead of building a
  shell command string; never dispatch untrusted input through a shell.
references: CWE-78

id: SAST-INJ-SQL_CONCAT-01
title: SQL statement built by string concatenation
severity: critical
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-89
owasp: A03:2021
pattern: ["'](SELECT|INSERT|UPDATE|DELETE)[^"']*["'][[:space:]]*(\+|%)
dialect: ere
tags: static
tags: quick
remediation: Use parameterised queries or an ORM that never interpolates request-derived
  data into SQL text.
references: CWE-89

id: SAST-INJ-CRLF_HEADER-01
title: Response header value built from request-derived data
severity: high
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-113
owasp: A03:2021
pattern: (setHeader|set_header)\([^)]*req(uest)?\.
dialect: ere
tags: static
remediation: Reject or strip CR/LF from any value placed into a response header, and
  prefer a framework API that rejects header-splitting characters outright.
references: CWE-113

id: SAST-INJ-HOST_HEADER_TRUST-01
title: Host header trusted to build a URL or redirect target
severity: medium
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-441
owasp: A03:2021
pattern: (request\.headers\.get\(["']Host["']\)|req\.headers\.host|HTTP_HOST\b|request\.headers\[["']Host["']\])
dialect: ere
tags: static
remediation: Build absolute URLs from a configured, trusted hostname rather than the
  request's Host header, which the client fully controls.
references: CWE-441

id: SAST-INJ-SSTI-01
title: Server-side template built from request-derived data
severity: critical
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-1336
owasp: A03:2021
pattern: (render_template_string\(|Template\([^)]*request\.|jinja2\.Template\()
dialect: ere
tags: static
remediation: Never compile a template string built from request-derived data; use a fixed
  template with request data passed only as render-context variables.
references: CWE-1336

id: SAST-INJ-OPEN_REDIRECT-01
title: Redirect target taken directly from request-derived data
severity: medium
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-601
owasp: A01:2021
pattern: (redirect\(request\.|res\.redirect\(req\.|response\.sendRedirect\(request\.getParameter)
dialect: ere
tags: static
remediation: Validate the redirect target against an allow-list of known-safe paths/hosts
  before honoring it, rather than redirecting to whatever the request supplied.
references: CWE-601

id: SAST-INJ-MASS_ASSIGNMENT-01
title: Whole request body bound directly to a model
severity: high
confidence: low
cwe: CWE-915
owasp: A08:2021
pattern: (\.update_attributes\(request\.|Model\(\*\*request\.|\.update\(\*\*request\.)
dialect: ere
tags: static
severity-floor: low
remediation: Bind only an explicit allow-list of fields from the request to the model,
  never the whole body, so a client cannot set fields it should never control (roles,
  ownership, verified flags).
references: CWE-915

id: SAST-INJ-XXE-01
title: XML parser configured to resolve external entities
severity: high
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-611
owasp: A05:2021
pattern: (resolve_entities[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*True|disallow-doctype-decl[^)]*[Ff]alse|IS_SUPPORTING_EXTERNAL_ENTITIES[^)]*true)
dialect: ere
tags: static
remediation: Disable external entity resolution and DTD processing on every XML parser
  that reads untrusted input; use the platform's documented hardened-parser configuration.
references: CWE-611
